@startuml
title DeploymentPlan — State Machine
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> DRAFT : createPlan()
DRAFT --> DRAFT : updatePlan()
DRAFT -[#gray,dashed]-> PENDING_APPROVAL : submitForApproval() <<planned>>
DRAFT --> APPROVED : review(APPROVED)
DRAFT --> REJECTED : review(REJECTED)
DRAFT --> CHANGES_REQUESTED : review(CHANGES_REQUESTED)

PENDING_APPROVAL --> APPROVED : review(APPROVED)
PENDING_APPROVAL --> REJECTED : review(REJECTED)
PENDING_APPROVAL --> CHANGES_REQUESTED : review(CHANGES_REQUESTED)
CHANGES_REQUESTED --> CHANGES_REQUESTED : updatePlan()
CHANGES_REQUESTED -[#gray,dashed]-> PENDING_APPROVAL : resubmit() <<planned>>

APPROVED --> DEPLOYING : deploy() [status == APPROVED]
DEPLOYING -[#gray,dashed]-> COMPLETED : allTasksSucceeded() <<planned>>
DEPLOYING -[#gray,dashed]-> FAILED : taskFailure() <<planned>>
FAILED -[#gray,dashed]-> ROLLED_BACK : rollbackApproved() <<planned>>

note right of PENDING_APPROVAL
  The enum and seed use this state, but there is
  no submit endpoint to reach it from a draft.
end note
note right of APPROVED
  The current review API accepts review requests
  without validating the plan's source state.
end note
note right of REJECTED
  A rejected plan remains recorded. A revised plan
  would be a new object, not a state transition here.
end note
note bottom of DEPLOYING
  The current deploy API sets the plan to DEPLOYING
  and its tasks to PENDING. An agent execution
  loop and completion/rollback transitions are absent.
end note

legend bottom
  Solid arrow = transition reachable through the current API.
  Dashed gray arrow = intended transition not implemented.
  DeploymentPlan records persist; no terminal node means no automatic deletion.
endlegend
@enduml
